# {{packageName}}

<!-- Badges go here, in the standard's order: registry version, Tests, Static
     analysis, License MIT -- but only the ones whose claim is true for THIS
     repository. A registry badge for a package the registry does not have
     renders as a broken "invalid" pill while asserting the package is
     installable, and a CI badge on a private repository answers 404 for every
     logged-out reader. Add a one-line note under them saying why any of the
     four is absent, so the next reader does not restore the count. -->

> {{humanName}} icons for the Ichava Laravel icon ecosystem.

Requires [`ichava/core`](https://github.com/ichava/core); targets PHP `^8.4.1 || ^8.5` on Laravel `^13`.

## Install

This pack requires [`ichava/core`](https://github.com/ichava/core) and nothing else. Nothing in the Ichava family is on Packagist yet, so the **application's** `composer.json` first names the repositories: core's [installation guide](https://github.com/ichava/core/blob/main/docs/installation.md#1-point-composer-at-the-repositories) holds the one block that lists them, core's dependencies included, and this pack's line in it is `https://github.com/{{packageName}}`.

Then require the pack:

```bash
composer require {{packageName}}
```

The service provider is discovered automatically. Core's [installation guide](https://github.com/ichava/core/blob/main/docs/installation.md) covers core's own setup.

## Quick start guide and usage

### Getting started

Seed the pack once after installing it, and again after upgrading it:

```bash
php artisan ichava::ichava-core.database seed --package={{packageName}}
```

The seed is not optional: until it runs the registry holds no rows for this pack and every lookup returns nothing. No configuration is needed; the pack ships no config file, and its settings live in `resources/assets/svg/config.json`.

### Usage

Icons are addressed as `{{packageName}}::<name>`. In Blade, through core's component:

```blade
<x-ichava::icon name="{{packageName}}::home" class="w-6 h-6" />
```

Or from PHP, through core's helper:

```blade
{{ ichava('{{packageName}}::home')->class('w-5 h-5') }}
```

See [Getting started](docs/getting-started.md) for the full walkthrough, and the [Documentation](#documentation) index below for everything else.

